---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'About Daily Prompt Hack',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:py-20 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <header class="mb-8 md:mb-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tighter tracking-tighter mb-4 font-heading dark:text-gray-200">
        About Daily Prompt Hack
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 text-lg">
        Advanced AI Architectures, Prompt Engineering Blueprints, and Generative Workflows
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">Our Mission</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        <strong>Daily Prompt Hack</strong> (<a href="https://prompt.storydailyview.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">prompt.storydailyview.com</a>) is an independent technical publication dedicated to prompt engineering, large language model (LLM) optimization, and production-ready generative AI workflows.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        We bridge the gap between human creative intent and deterministic machine execution. Rather than superficial prompt collections, our focus is on robust system architectures—including structured markdown frameworks, few-shot conditioning, chain-of-thought protocols, and role-based persona designs—that deliver reproducible, high-yield results across modern AI platforms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">What We Cover</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
        <li>
          <strong>Structured Prompt Engineering:</strong> Few-shot prompt patterns, chain-of-thought methodologies, schema enforcement, and delimiter-driven token control.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>LLM Optimization & Reasoning:</strong> Context-window management, temperature tuning, system instruction architecture, and hallucination mitigation strategies.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Content & Script Reverse Engineering:</strong> Viral script frameworks, high-retention storytelling blueprints, and audience-tailored narrative prompting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Enterprise & Automation Pipelines:</strong> Automated API prompt chaining, structured JSON/YAML generation for backend feeds, and repeatable batch workflows.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cross-Model Benchmarking:</strong> Comparative behavior, formatting nuances, and prompt migration across ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and open-source models.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Editorial & Engineering Standards</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Every prompt template, parameter recommendation, and automation architecture published on Daily Prompt Hack is rigorously tested across multiple model checkpoints. We prioritize reproducibility, deterministic output structures, and ethical AI deployment principles to support developers, content creators, and enterprise architects worldwide.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
